<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Resazurin                                                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;940.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components and autoclave under a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20, v/v) gas mixture. After cooling, aseptically and anaerobically, add the following solutions from anaerobic stocks (filtersterilized):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Vitamin solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=898">898</a>)                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 8% NaHCO<sub>3</sub> solution                                   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;50.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Dispense the medium into culture vessels (e.g., 5 ml medium in Hungate tubes) under a H<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20, v/v) gas stream and seal with butyl stoppers. Prior to inoculation, add per liter the following solutions (autoclaved and stored under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 5% Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solution                       </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 5% L-Cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O solution               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
After inoculation, pressurize the inoculated culture vessels to 100 kPa H<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20, v/v).       <br>
